\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * This runs inside a Google Sheet as an Apps Script Web App. It acts\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * as the database and API for the booking page (booking.html).\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * SETUP (about 10 minutes, one time):\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * 1. Go to https://sheets.google.com and create a new blank spreadsheet.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *    Name it something like "Tutoring Bookings".\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * 2. Create two tabs (right-click the tab bar at the bottom):\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *      Tab 1 named exactly:  Accounts\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *        Row 1 headers: Email | Name | Phone | PIN | CreatedAt\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *      Tab 2 named exactly:  Availability\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *        Row 1 headers: ID | Date | Time | Duration | Booked | ParentEmail | ParentName | ParentPhone | StudentName | Note | ReminderSent\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * 3. In the Sheet, go to Extensions > Apps Script.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * 4. Delete any starter code in Code.gs and paste in this entire file.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * 5. Change ADMIN_KEY below to a passcode only you know.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * 6. Click Deploy > New deployment > gear icon > Web app.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *      - Execute as: Me\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *      - Who has access: Anyone\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * 7. Click Deploy, authorize when prompted, then copy the Web App URL\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *    (it ends in /exec).\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * 8. Open booking.html, find the line "var API_URL = ..." near the top\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *    of the <script> tag, and paste your URL in between the quotes.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * 9. NEW \'97 one-time reminder setup: in the Apps Script editor, click\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *    the clock icon (Triggers) on the left, + Add Trigger, choose\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *    function "sendSessionReminders", Event source "Time-driven",\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *    Type "Hour timer", Every hour, then Save. It'll ask to authorize\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *    Gmail/MailApp access \'97 approve it. This is what sends the\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *    24-hour-out reminder emails automatically from here on.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * If you already have this sheet deployed and are just updating the\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * code: your "Availability" tab needs an 11th column header, exactly\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * "ReminderSent", in cell K1. Existing rows can be left blank there \'97\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * blank is treated the same as "not sent yet".\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * That's it \'97 the booking page will now read and write to this sheet.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * You can always open the Sheet directly to see everything at a glance.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  *\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * UPDATING THIS SCRIPT LATER:\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * If you edit this code after your first deployment (like adding the\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * email notifications below), saving it in the Apps Script editor is\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2  * NOT enough by itself \'97 go to Deploy > Manage deployments, click the\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
